-- Nesting. A binder on a heading covers every definition in every section
-- beneath it. A child re-declaring an ancestor's name is a DISTINCT binder that
-- shadows within the child's subtree. A sibling with no binder of its own sees
-- the ancestor's.

§ `top`
    GIVEN foo IS A NUMBER

GIVETH A NUMBER
`top reader` MEANS foo PLUS 1

§§ `child`
    GIVEN foo IS A STRING

GIVETH A STRING
`child reader` MEANS foo

§§ `sibling`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`sibling reader` MEANS foo PLUS 2
